1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:03,860
This is real footage from
a US Navy fighter jet.

2
00:00:03,910 --> 00:00:06,233
The Pentagon released it officially.

3
00:00:06,386 --> 00:00:10,958
And to this day, it calls what
you're looking at... unidentified.

4
00:00:11,300 --> 00:00:13,834
But this video isn't the strange part.

5
00:00:14,028 --> 00:00:19,732
Earlier that same day, two Navy jets flew down
to look at this object with their own eyes.

6
00:00:19,933 --> 00:00:23,122
One of those pilots later
told Congress, under oath,

7
00:00:23,172 --> 00:00:26,424
that it was far superior
to anything we have.

8
00:00:26,653 --> 00:00:28,509
This is what they described.

9
00:00:29,200 --> 00:00:31,267
November, 2004.

10
00:00:31,559 --> 00:00:36,496
The aircraft carrier USS Nimitz is training
off the coast of Southern California.

11
00:00:36,546 --> 00:00:40,606
Its escort, the cruiser USS
Princeton, has a problem.

12
00:00:40,656 --> 00:00:44,032
For more than two weeks, its
radar has been tracking objects

13
00:00:44,082 --> 00:00:49,052
that appear above eighty thousand feet,
then drop to around twenty thousand.

14
00:00:49,157 --> 00:00:51,919
That's far higher than airliners fly.

15
00:00:52,300 --> 00:00:55,281
On November fourteenth,
Commander David Fravor,

16
00:00:55,331 --> 00:00:59,718
who leads the Black Aces fighter
squadron, takes off for a training fight.

17
00:00:59,898 --> 00:01:04,190
Two F/A-18F Super Hornets,
two people in each.

18
00:01:04,350 --> 00:01:07,258
Flying the other jet is
Lieutenant Alex Dietrich.

19
00:01:07,469 --> 00:01:10,182
Mid-flight, the exercise is called off.

20
00:01:10,345 --> 00:01:14,227
There's something out there.
And they are the closest jets.

21
00:01:14,800 --> 00:01:20,138
The sea is calm. Clear sky,
light wind, no waves breaking.

22
00:01:20,433 --> 00:01:22,570
Then they notice whitewater.

23
00:01:22,829 --> 00:01:27,192
A patch of churning sea, as if
something is just below the surface.

24
00:01:27,316 --> 00:01:29,722
And above it, moving
abruptly over the water,

25
00:01:29,772 --> 00:01:34,232
is what Fravor later described
as a white Tic Tac object.

26
00:01:34,414 --> 00:01:38,782
No wings. No rotors. Nothing
he could see holding it up.

27
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:43,392
Fravor drops down for a closer
look. And the object responds.

28
00:01:43,486 --> 00:01:48,054
In his words, it aligned itself with
his aircraft, and began to climb.

29
00:01:48,236 --> 00:01:49,922
He cuts across to meet it.

30
00:01:50,025 --> 00:01:55,460
Then, he says, it rapidly accelerated
in front of them... and disappeared.

31
00:01:55,635 --> 00:01:58,986
They turn back to the
whitewater. That's gone too.

32
00:02:00,200 --> 00:02:03,718
Then the radio. The ship
had found it again.

33
00:02:03,768 --> 00:02:07,478
At their planned meeting point.
Roughly sixty miles away.

34
00:02:07,528 --> 00:02:09,206
In less than a minute.

35
00:02:10,400 --> 00:02:15,509
Back on the carrier, another crew launches.
This time, with a targeting camera.

36
00:02:15,830 --> 00:02:19,927
They find an object, and record about
ninety seconds of infrared video.

37
00:02:20,174 --> 00:02:22,785
That's this clip. The
one the Navy released.

38
00:02:23,060 --> 00:02:25,350
Here's what most uploads don't tell you.

39
00:02:25,563 --> 00:02:28,671
This crew never saw the
object with their own eyes.

40
00:02:28,754 --> 00:02:31,152
And this isn't Fravor's close encounter.

41
00:02:31,202 --> 00:02:35,192
It's a later flight, a camera
locked onto a distant target.

42
00:02:35,400 --> 00:02:38,323
At the end, the object slips out of frame.

43
00:02:38,442 --> 00:02:40,835
Some see a sudden burst of speed.

44
00:02:41,050 --> 00:02:43,704
Skeptics say the camera
simply lost its lock.

45
00:02:43,754 --> 00:02:46,370
The footage alone can't settle it.

46
00:02:46,546 --> 00:02:49,845
And that matters...
because of the next video.

47
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:56,562
This one is called Go Fast.

48
00:02:56,926 --> 00:03:01,254
A Navy jet, off the coast
of Florida, January 2015.

49
00:03:01,562 --> 00:03:05,322
It looks like something skimming
the ocean at incredible speed.

50
00:03:05,372 --> 00:03:07,992
And the crew are clearly excited.

51
00:03:08,277 --> 00:03:11,809
But in 2025, the Pentagon's
UFO office, AARO,

52
00:03:11,859 --> 00:03:15,780
ran the numbers from the
camera's own readouts.

53
00:03:15,830 --> 00:03:20,791
The object was about thirteen thousand
feet up. Nowhere near the water.

54
00:03:20,852 --> 00:03:24,019
The sea rushing past is
the jet's own motion.

55
00:03:24,349 --> 00:03:29,291
AARO's estimate? Somewhere between
five and ninety-two miles an hour.

56
00:03:29,386 --> 00:03:30,874
Moving with the wind.

57
00:03:31,142 --> 00:03:36,478
In their words: high confidence that the
object did not move at anomalous speeds.

58
00:03:37,200 --> 00:03:39,410
So a video can fool you.

59
00:03:39,650 --> 00:03:44,627
And that's exactly why the Nimitz case is
different. It doesn't rest on a video.

60
00:03:44,709 --> 00:03:50,126
It rests on four trained aviators,
two jets, and a warship's radar.

61
00:03:50,201 --> 00:03:52,537
All describing the same thing.

62
00:03:53,600 --> 00:03:58,319
And twenty years later...
the reports haven't stopped.

63
00:03:58,369 --> 00:04:00,476
Pilots. Sailors. Drone crews.

64
00:04:00,643 --> 00:04:06,762
In just over a year, the Pentagon's
UFO office logged 757 new reports.

65
00:04:06,812 --> 00:04:09,320
Most of them never reach the public.

66
00:04:09,400 --> 00:04:15,824
In February 2026, the President ordered
federal agencies to release their UFO files.

67
00:04:15,874 --> 00:04:21,938
Since May, the Pentagon has published
seven batches, at war.gov/UFO.

68
00:04:21,988 --> 00:04:24,780
The latest came out on
October twenty-third.

69
00:04:25,080 --> 00:04:27,711
Documents only. No new video.

70
00:04:32,400 --> 00:04:37,033
In it, federal agents at a sensitive
site in the western United States

71
00:04:37,083 --> 00:04:41,416
report a matte black triangle,
up to fifteen feet across.

72
00:04:41,692 --> 00:04:46,456
It rises above a ridge. Hovers.
Then drops into a canyon.

73
00:04:46,869 --> 00:04:49,110
No sound. No exhaust.

74
00:04:49,485 --> 00:04:52,118
The next morning, a search finds nothing.

75
00:04:52,286 --> 00:04:56,330
But the two government reports don't
even agree on how long it lasted.

76
00:04:56,649 --> 00:05:00,064
The AARO memo says more
than thirty seconds.

77
00:05:00,114 --> 00:05:02,846
The FBI write-up says about three.

78
00:05:03,106 --> 00:05:05,238
And there's no video at all.

79
00:05:06,200 --> 00:05:10,747
Twenty-two years on, nobody has
officially explained the Tic Tac.

80
00:05:11,033 --> 00:05:14,286
Alex Dietrich, who flew the
other jet, put it simply.

81
00:05:14,522 --> 00:05:16,112
We don't know what it was.

82
00:05:16,196 --> 00:05:19,946
That's not proof of aliens. But
it isn't explained, either.

83
00:05:20,043 --> 00:05:22,660
Four people saw something
they couldn't name.

84
00:05:22,794 --> 00:05:24,987
And nobody has named it since.

85
00:05:25,339 --> 00:05:27,711
If you want the next file the
moment it drops, subscribe.

86
00:05:27,761 --> 00:05:31,223
I'll keep reading them,
so you don't have to.
